# Navigation and Layout Structure

## Header Navigation
The main navigation is implemented in the dashboard header with the following structure:

```jsx
<header className="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-[99999]">
  {/* Logo */}
  {/* Navigation Links */}
  {/* User Menu Dropdown */}
</header>
```

### User Menu Dropdown
- Triggered by clicking user avatar
- Contains "Edit Profile" and "Sign Out" options
- Uses z-index layering to appear above other elements
- Closes when clicking outside

## Layout Components

### Search/Filter Bar
- Sticky positioning below header
- Contains search input and filter dropdowns
- Responsive design for mobile/desktop
- Filter categories: Type, Specialty, Location, Duration

### Main Content Layout
The main content area uses a two-column layout:

```jsx
<main className="flex-1 flex flex-col md:flex-row">
  <Sidebar /> {/* 1/4 width on desktop */}
  <MainContent /> {/* 3/4 width on desktop */}
</main>
```

### Sidebar Features
- Collapsible on mobile
- Sticky positioning on desktop
- Contains:
  - Stats/Quick Actions
  - Opportunity List
  - Sort Controls

### Z-Index Hierarchy
```css
Header: z-[99999]
User Dropdown: z-[99999]
Search Bar: z-[99998]
Sort Dropdown: z-[9999]
Sidebar: z-20
```

## Responsive Breakpoints
- Mobile: < 768px
- Tablet: 768px - 1024px
- Desktop: > 1024px

## Component Visibility
- Navigation links: Hidden on mobile, visible on desktop
- Sidebar: Collapsible on mobile, fixed on desktop
- Search/Filter: Stacks vertically on mobile, horizontal on desktop

